 "description": "§28 step 2: WHERE inside CurSkyTarget the time goes, broken out per postfix. Shares only -- sixteen simultaneous arms inflate every row by Circinus's per-call transpile cost, so these numbers rank the postfixes against each other and must not be quoted as any one postfix's cost; perf_parents.json is the file for that. The parent arm is kept so the sum of the children can be checked against it: a large unexplained gap means the time is somewhere nobody armed, which is how §27 lost three days to a lazily-built polygon set. ARMS NAMED `Apply`: the fourteen sky stages stopped being Harmony postfixes when the sky-target composite (§29) took them over, and the arms here still named `Postfix`, so thirteen of sixteen resolved nothing and reported the whole sky chain as free. The *_patched pins are what caught it and are the reason every arm added here must keep one.",
